cff-version: 1.2.0
# meta-id: 4d799635c7faa545
title: BearingNode Lab
message: >-
  If you use or refer to this work, please cite it using the metadata in
  this file.
type: software
authors:
  - name: BearingNode
    website: https://www.bearingnode.com
repository-code: https://github.com/BearingNode/bearingnode-lab
url: https://www.bearingnode.com

# This file describes the lab as a whole, not any one workstream — it is
# parsed root-only, so there is no per-workstream citation file and this one
# has to hold for all of them. The abstract below therefore names no
# workstream, so it stays accurate as workstreams are added.
abstract: >-
  BearingNode Lab is BearingNode's public engineering work on observability,
  lineage and governance across AI, software, and data and information,
  treating the three as related. Its organising term of art is Data and Information Observability (D/I O11y): "The body of knowledge
  and practices for monitoring the health, performance, and organisational
  impact of Data and Information assets, as well as the capabilities to steward
  those assets." Output is published per workstream as reference
  implementations, specification proposals and upstream contributions, and is
  intended as reference material.

# Keywords accrete over time: the abstract stays stable, but this list grows
# as workstreams are added, each contributing the ecosystem terms a reader or
# a model would filter on for that work. Nothing is removed.
keywords:
  - observability
  - data lineage
  - OpenLineage
  - OpenTelemetry
  - Model Context Protocol
  - AI governance
  - AI observability
  - data and information observability

# The `license` key takes an SPDX identifier from the SPDX licence list, and
# will not accept a `LicenseRef-` value. The BearingNode Community and
# Research Licence is a bespoke instrument with no SPDX list entry, so the
# `license` key is deliberately omitted and `license-url` carries the position
# instead. Omitting it is correct; populating it with anything from the SPDX
# list would be a false statement about the licence.
license-url: https://github.com/BearingNode/bearingnode-lab/blob/main/LICENSE.md

# CalVer, not SemVer. `0.1.0` would imply an API-compatibility contract this
# lab does not offer; a date tells a citing reader when the state existed,
# which is the question they actually have. Lab editions are `YYYY.MM` and
# carry no workstream name. A one-off state cited externally (an upstream
# reply, a blog link) gets its own descriptive tag instead, so a workstream is
# named where it is the point and omitted where it is not.
#
# KEEP THE QUOTES. Unquoted, YAML reads 2026.07 as a float, and a later 2026.10
# would silently become 2026.1.
version: "2026.08"

# date-released must be the actual date this edition is cut, not the date
# this file was last drafted. Set it from the same cut recorded in the
# Editions table in README.md.
date-released: "2026-08-10"
